    "Connector grouping: the vertical PORT.A text beside left-edge pins 13 and 15 suggests the PORT.A box may describe those same signals rather than a separate physical connector; it was transcribed as its own connector."
  ],
  "notes": "Left-edge numbers sit in colored circles keyed by a PIN legend (ADC1/ADC2/no ADC/POWER), so they are GPIO numbers kept as labels as printed. Right-edge numbers printed beside board names (Tx 43, Rx 44, Boot 0) are kept as functions; Rst/EN uses the control name EN. nWAKE is printed as a small n above WAKE. Buttons, IR, buzzer, LEDs, SD, IMU, RTC, mic and USB D-/D+ GPIO notes are not wiring points and were skipped."
